# Software Description

## Objective

Develop a Super Mario game.

## Core Features

Mario can move left, right, and jump using the arrow keys.
Mario interacts with blocks: when hit, a mushroom appears.
Mushrooms move left and fall to the ground. If Mario touches the mushroom, it disappears and adds to the score.
Enemies move left and right randomly. If Mario touches an enemy, he loses.
Mario¡¯s goal is to reach the flagpole at the end of the game. When Mario touches the flagpole, the game ends.
Game settings:

There is a ground where Mario and enemies can stand and walk.
A single block appears above Mario's starting position, and hitting it releases a mushroom.
The score increases by 1 every second. It increases by 100 when Mario hits a block, by 1000 when Mario touches a mushroom, and by 10000 when Mario reaches the flagpole.

## Language

Use python to develop a pygame application.
### Data Storage

Data will be stored in local text files.
functional requirements
[OUTPUT] ## general overview of the project Develop a Super Mario game. ## software functional requirements 1. **Character Movement**    - Mario shall be able to move left and right using the left and right arrow keys.    - Mario shall be able to jump using the up arrow key. 2. **Block Interaction**    - When Mario hits a block, a mushroom shall appear above the block.    - The block shall be interactive and respond to Mario's action. 3. **Mushroom Behavior**    - The mushroom shall move left and fall to the ground after being released from the block.    - If Mario touches the mushroom, it shall disappear and add to the player's score. 4. **Enemy Behavior**    - Enemies shall move left and right randomly within the game environment.    - If Mario touches an enemy, the game shall register a loss for Mario. 5. **Game Objective**    - Mario's goal shall be to reach the flagpole at the end of the game.    - When Mario touches the flagpole, the game shall end. 6. **Game Settings**    - The game shall include a ground area where Mario and enemies can stand and walk.    - A single block shall appear above Mario's starting position, which can be hit to release a mushroom. 7. **Scoring System**    - The score shall increase by 1 every second.    - The score shall increase by 100 when Mario hits a block.    - The score shall increase by 1000 when Mario touches a mushroom.    - The score shall increase by 10000 when Mario reaches the flagpole. 8. **Data Storage**    - Game data, including scores and settings, shall be stored in local text files. [/OUTPUT]
